<section class="section theme-dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="label content-section__label">About</p>
    <h1 class="content-section__heading" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); max-width: none;">Mikael Viima</h1>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>
        Mikael Viima is the literary name of <strong>Manne Mikael Laukkanen</strong>,
        a Finnish writer with a PhD in psychology and a background spanning criminal
        profiling research, technology, data and music.
      </p>
      <p>
        His first crime novel, <strong>Verijälki</strong>, was published by WSOY in
        2022. <strong>Rekyyli</strong> followed in 2023. In 2024, Otava published his
        nonfiction book <strong>Vaaralliset gurut</strong> under his real name.
      </p>
      <p>He now writes poetry and fiction for a wider English-speaking readership.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap about-teaser">
    <div>
      <div class="portrait-placeholder">
        <p class="portrait-placeholder__text">{{ author.portrait.alt }} — portrait pending</p>
      </div>
      <p class="photo-credit">{{ author.portrait.credit }}</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="content-section__heading">Psychology explains less than people hope. Literature can sometimes get closer.</h2>
      <div class="content-section__body">
        <p>
          Viima's doctoral work concerned the profiling of serial criminals. He has
          also spent decades working with data, software and large information
          systems across industries, in global settings.
        </p>
        <p>The combination has left a mark.</p>
        <p>One discipline asks what a person is likely to do.</p>
        <p>Another asks what the system is actually doing.</p>
        <p>Writing gets to ask the more uncomfortable question:</p>
        <p><strong>What if both descriptions are wrong?</strong></p>
        <p>
          His fiction and poetry move repeatedly through psychology, desire, love,
          memory, aging, science, mortality, art, class, power, politics, manipulation
          and damage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="content-section__heading">Why Mikael Viima</h2>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>&ldquo;Mikael&rdquo; is part of his real name.</p>
      <p>&ldquo;Viima&rdquo; is a Finnish word associated with a cold, cutting wind.</p>
      <p>
        The name began as the identity used for fiction. It now serves as the main
        literary identity for fiction and poetry in international markets.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight theme-steel">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="content-section__heading">Why write?</h2>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>Because some things still seem unsaid.</p>
      <p>Or said badly.</p>
      <p>Or softened until they no longer resemble the thing itself.</p>
      <p>The poems and novels begin there.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

